**Step 5, properties and pre-scan.** 5.1 Over `<main sha>..HEAD`: 0 non-ASCII bytes added (`LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c -E '^\+.*[^ -~]'`, planted control reads 1), also in commit messages; no TAB/CR added; no brief-number token (letter B plus digits) in an added line or message (planted `B667` reported); no person's name, no decision-card id, no percent sign (own regex; planted controls); no `.only/.skip/.todo/xit/retry/continue-on-error/codeql/lgtm` added (planted); `/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks git -c .gitleaks.toml --log-opts=<main sha>..HEAD` rc 0 AFTER a canary (a random `ghp_`-shaped token in a scratch repo under `session-tools/b823/`) fires rc 1, chained with `&&` in `bash -c`. 5.2 **CodeQL pre-scan for both thresholds (a PR must add NO NEW high-or-higher alert, test code included; ruleset has a second `alerts_threshold = errors`),** line by line over every added line: say what each new `fs` call sinks (path origin, whether it is derived from `os.tmpdir()`/`mkdtemp`/`dir`/a parameter), that no `child_process`, regex-from-input, network, env or log was added, and that the number of sinks (writes of a path from a parameter) per file is no higher than before. **The new head's CodeQL is UNMEASURED until the PR analyses finish.** 5.3 Neighbours: re-run every file of 3.2 after the last edit, `Tests:` equal.
**Step 6, jest whole-suite proof.** One lock ticket per run, tags `b823-build-<step>` (`-base`, `-nb`, `-mut`, `-verify`), `ls -la` of `queue-jest/` before and after each. `b823-build-verify` = the plain `npm run verify -- --maxWorkers=2` at the FINAL head: `VERDICT: PASS`, `verify-suite: expectation - tests=<n> suites=<m>` equal to the counts file's pair at the head (5170 / 307 unless re-stamped), `Tests:`/`Test Suites:` the same pair. If ANY pair differs: STOP naming both figures; do NOT add or delete a cell and do NOT regenerate the file. A red cell outside your four files: STOP naming it, no re-run into green (one recorded rerun only of a cell whose ticket carries a flake label; this work carries none). If jest is not startable (load1 at or above 7 for 60 minutes): do the light work (Steps 1, 2, the probes that need no jest), report PARTIAL "jest UNMEASURED"; never commit an unmeasured change.
**Step 7, push, or PARTIAL.** Everything proven: `ls-remote origin refs/heads/b823/nexusai-873-811-test-alerts` empty (else STOP). From the clone under `/bin/bash`: `git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/b823/nexusai-873-811-test-alerts` (new branch, plain; never `--force`/`--force-with-lease`/`+refspec`; publickey denial is transport, retry 5 times; GH013, "protected branch", "rejected", non-fast-forward are STOPs: say the message exactly). Read the ref back with `ls-remote`. Then GET only, bounded, heartbeat: `compare/<main sha>...<head>` (ahead <n>, files subset of A); `actions/runs?head_sha=<head>` every 30 s for up to 5 minutes, print name/event/status/conclusion (expect `npm-audit | push` and no `Deploy demo`; a run named as a workflow FILE PATH or `startup_failure` is a STOP; zero runs is valid: say which); `pulls?state=open` no PR for your branch; `code-scanning/analyses?ref=refs/heads/b823/nexusai-873-811-test-alerts` count. You never dispatch or re-run a workflow, never POST or PATCH. **PARTIAL:** if a Step cannot be shown, push nothing unproven; a change that is not proven is never on a pushed branch (a local commit may exist, unpushed); a subset of sites that ARE proven may be pushed alone if the rest are left byte-unchanged and the verify reads PASS.

